<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Statute of Westminster Adoption Act 1947</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1947</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Statute of Westminster Adoption Act 1947 was passed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> Parliament under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-fraser">Peter Fraser</a>'s Labour government to adopt the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/statute-of-westminster-1931">Statute of Westminster 1931</a>. Together with a British act passed at New Zealand's request, it gave the New Zealand Parliament full power to make its own laws, including amending its constitution, and is regarded as marking New Zealand's legal independence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/statute-of-westminster-adoption-act-1947.jpg" alt="Statute of Westminster Adoption Act 1947" width="320" height="297" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_New_Zealand_(1911%E2%80%931956).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
